WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:12.930
A covered put would be

2
00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:14.640
considered by someone
who would like to

3
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:18.300
derive additional income
from a short stock position.

4
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.180
A covered put allows
the investor to

5
00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:24.060
hold a short equity
position while

6
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.430
simultaneously receiving
the premium from

7
00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:30.490
selling an equal amount of
put options against it.

8
00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:34.815
The covered put writer is bearish

9
00:00:34.815 --> 00:00:36.890
on the stocks
long-term potential,

10
00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:38.370
but is willing to forego

11
00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.460
a stock's downside below

12
00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:42.950
the strike during the
life of the option,

13
00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:46.330
in order to receive the
proceeds of the put premium.

14
00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:50.100
The covered put writer
benefits from time decay,

15
00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.200
from a reduction in volatility,

16
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.809
and if the stock decreases

17
00:00:53.809 --> 00:00:56.285
its dividend before expiration.

18
00:00:56.285 --> 00:00:59.390
It should be noted that
the combined position has

19
00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:02.510
a similar profile to
that of a short call.

20
00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:05.030
The covered put writer remains

21
00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:07.985
exposed to any upside in
the underlying shares,

22
00:01:07.985 --> 00:01:11.790
meaning his loss
potential is unlimited.